//! Sorted and lower cased, so a lookup is one binary search with the candidate folded
//! the same way. One table rather than five, because the classes are not disjoint and
//! five tables would store the overlapping words more than once and then have to decide
//! which answer wins. A mask of zero means the word is spelled by some rule and is in no
//! class, which makes it matchable as a literal and transparent everywhere else.

